      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "simplified": "\n",
      "traditional": "\n",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "Xiao Bao: Grandma, we took a taxi home today and it was extremely fast."
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "simplified": "奶奶：什么“快死了”？小孩子不要乱说话。",
      "traditional": "奶奶：什麼“快死了”？小孩子不要亂說話。",
      "pinyin": "nǎi nai shén me kuài sǐ le xiǎo hái zi bú yào luàn shuō huà",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "simplified": "\n",
      "traditional": "\n",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "Grandma: What do you mean by “about to die”? Don’t talk nonsense."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "simplified": "小宝：可是爸爸每天回家都说“累死了”，",
      "traditional": "小寶：可是爸爸每天回家都說“累死了”，",
      "pinyin": "xiǎo bǎo kě shì bà ba měi tiān huí jiā dōu shuō lèi sǐ le",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "simplified": "妈妈也常常说“忙死了”。",
      "traditional": "媽媽也常常說“忙死了”。",
      "pinyin": "mā ma yě cháng cháng shuō máng sǐ le",
      "english": "Xiao Bao: But dad says “extremely tired” every day when he comes back home."
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "simplified": "今天出租车司机叔叔开车开得非常快，为什么不可以说“快死了”？",
      "traditional": "今天出租車司機叔叔開車開得非常快，為什麼不可以說“快死了”？",
      "pinyin": "jīn tiān chū zū chē sī jī shū shu kāi chē kāi de fēi cháng kuài wèi shén me bù kě yǐ shuō kuài sǐ le",
      "english": "And mom often says “extremely busy”."
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "simplified": "\n",
      "traditional": "\n",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "The taxi driver drove very fast today, so why can't I say “extremely fast”?"
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "simplified": "奶奶：那你就说“非常快”。",
      "traditional": "奶奶：那你就說“非常快”。",
      "pinyin": "nǎi nai nà nǐ jiù shuō fēi cháng kuài",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "simplified": "“快死了”听起来像人快要死了，以后不要说了，乖小宝。",
      "traditional": "“快死了”聽起來像人快要死了，以後不要說了，乖小寶。",
      "pinyin": "kuài sǐ le tīng qǐ lái xiàng rén kuài yào sǐ le yǐ hòu bú yào shuō le guāi xiǎo bǎo",
      "english": "Grandma: Then you can say “very fast”."
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "simplified": "\n",
      "traditional": "\n",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "“Extremely fast” sounds like someone is about to die. Don’t say it anymore, sweetie."
    },
    {
